Statistics are collected for indexes built by a schema change, before that
schema change commits.

Covers:
  - CREATE INDEX populates sqlite_stat1 with no explicit ANALYZE
  - those statistics are visible on every node, not just the master
  - ALTER TABLE adding an index does the same; indexes it did not rebuild
    are read from the old table and keep the same statistics
  - altering an index definition refreshes its statistics and moves the
    row under its old name aside with the rest of the table's old rows
  - an existing index that was never analyzed gets statistics when another
    index is created
  - a datacopy-driven rebuild does not lose existing statistics
  - DROP INDEX does not resurrect statistics
  - the analyze_new_indexes tunable disables the behavior
  - a full REBUILD, which has no schema-change plan, analyzes every index
  - with sc_analyze_required, a schema change fails if the analyze cannot
    run; without it, the schema change proceeds without stats
  - with stats for a new unselective index, the planner keeps using the
    selective index; without them it switches to the new one

Runs standalone or against a cluster; the per-node checks degrade to a
single-host check when there is only one node.
